Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:

##### Sets and Indices

- $S = \{\text{I}, \text{II}\}$: set of schools, indexed by $s$
- $N = \{\text{N01}, \text{N02}, \ldots, \text{N31}\}$: set of neighborhoods, indexed by $n$

##### Parameters

- $\text{Cap}_s$: capacity of school $s$
  - $\text{Cap}_\text{I} = 2028$
  - $\text{Cap}_\text{II} = 1560$
- $\text{PopW}_n$: white population in neighborhood $n$ (see table below)
- $\text{PopNW}_n$: nonwhite population in neighborhood $n$ (see table below)
- $\text{Dist}_{s,n}$: distance in miles from school $s$ to neighborhood $n$ (see table below)
- District-wide white percentage: $p_W = 0.6$, nonwhite percentage $p_{NW} = 0.4$
- Allowed deviation: $0.1$ (10 percentage points)

##### Decision Variables

- $x_{s,n}^W \geq 0$: number of white students assigned from neighborhood $n$ to school $s$ (continuous)
- $x_{s,n}^{NW} \geq 0$: number of nonwhite students assigned from neighborhood $n$ to school $s$ (continuous)

##### Objective

Minimize total student-miles traveled:
$$
\min \sum_{s \in S} \sum_{n \in N} \text{Dist}_{s,n} \left( x_{s,n}^W + x_{s,n}^{NW} \right)
$$

##### Constraints

1. **Neighborhood population assignment:**  
   For all $n \in N$,
   $$
   \sum_{s \in S} x_{s,n}^W = \text{PopW}_n
   $$
   $$
   \sum_{s \in S} x_{s,n}^{NW} = \text{PopNW}_n
   $$

2. **School capacity:**  
   For all $s \in S$,
   $$
   \sum_{n \in N} \left( x_{s,n}^W + x_{s,n}^{NW} \right) \leq \text{Cap}_s
   $$

3. **Racial balance at each school:**  
   For all $s \in S$,
   $$
   0.5 \leq \frac{\sum_{n \in N} x_{s,n}^W}{\sum_{n \in N} \left( x_{s,n}^W + x_{s,n}^{NW} \right)} \leq 0.7
   $$
   (i.e., white percentage at each school must be within $[0.5, 0.7]$)

4. **Nonnegativity:**  
   $$
   x_{s,n}^W \geq 0,\quad x_{s,n}^{NW} \geq 0 \qquad \forall s \in S, n \in N
   $$

---

